# Federated app routing

The Shell hosts this remote at `/apps/{slug}/*`. Root-absolute React Router paths work in Dev Shell only if Dev Shell is also mounted there. After publish, `to="/records"` leaves the app.

## Required

- Route paths are **segments**, no leading slash: `path="records"`, `path="records/:id"`, `index` for the landing page.
- Every `Link`, `NavLink`, `navigate()`, and `<Navigate>` uses `useAppPath('records')` or `useAppBasePath()` from `src/lib/useAppPath.ts`.
- Dev Shell must nest the app under `/apps/:appSlug/*` (see `src/dev/DevShell.tsx`) so local URLs match production.
- Manifest `routes[].path` values are segments (`home`), never `/my-app/home`.

## Forbidden

```tsx
<Link to="/records">
navigate('/records')
<Route path="/records" />
```

## Correct

```tsx
const recordsPath = useAppPath('records');
<Link to={recordsPath}>Records</Link>
navigate(useAppPath('records/123'));
<Route path="records" element={<Records />} />
<Route path="records/:id" element={<RecordDetail />} />
```

Do not use relative `to="records"` from a sibling page — from `/apps/slug/home` that becomes `/apps/slug/home/records`. Always prefix with `useAppPath`.
